WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.291 --> 00:00:02.762
- No one is perfect at everything.

00:00:02.762 --> 00:00:05.179
And we're all made to
be perfectly imperfect.

00:00:05.179 --> 00:00:08.815
I was rejected but it was the
best rejection ever for me

00:00:08.815 --> 00:00:10.854
to lead me in a different direction,

00:00:10.854 --> 00:00:13.345
the direction where I'm
heading towards right now.

00:00:13.345 --> 00:00:16.357
You learn way more when you
fail than when you succeed.

00:00:16.357 --> 00:00:18.417
That's something I can guarantee you on.

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:21.173
You want to tell stories and
you want something that can last

00:00:21.173 --> 00:00:23.877
longer than just a one hit wonder.

00:00:23.877 --> 00:00:25.509
- What's up Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:25.509 --> 00:00:26.896
My one word is believe,

00:00:26.896 --> 00:00:28.967
and I believe that you have the ability

00:00:28.967 --> 00:00:31.530
to do something special
that can change the planet.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.913
So, to help you on your journey today,

00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:34.934
we're going to learn from
YouTuber and entrepreneur

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:38.798
Michelle Phan, and my take on
her top ten rules for success.

00:00:38.798 --> 00:00:40.659
Rule number six is my personal favorite,

00:00:40.659 --> 00:00:44.826
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:46.482 --> 00:00:49.232
(uplifting tune)

00:00:56.404 --> 00:00:59.622
- I came from a mother and
father who are both immigrants,

00:00:59.622 --> 00:01:00.837
didn't speak English,

00:01:00.837 --> 00:01:02.440
so I had to learn English on my own,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.639
I had to learn it through
TV and through school

00:01:04.639 --> 00:01:06.418
and I had to learn how to
speak Vietnamese at home.

00:01:06.418 --> 00:01:07.838
Everything that I know of today

00:01:07.838 --> 00:01:09.570
I had to teach myself,

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.973
I had to learn from other people,

00:01:11.973 --> 00:01:12.970
bring on mentors,

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.701
and also adapting.

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:15.869
Silencing my mind,

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:19.527
and just observing quietly
and adapting to that.

00:01:19.527 --> 00:01:21.057
Even when I was doing YouTube,

00:01:21.057 --> 00:01:22.628
everyone thought I was crazy,

00:01:22.628 --> 00:01:25.025
everyone thought I was stupid,

00:01:25.025 --> 00:01:26.465
like, they literally
said, oh, that's so dumb,

00:01:26.465 --> 00:01:28.067
you could never make money on YouTube,

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.120
why would you do that?

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.364
Why not just go get a corporate job?

00:01:31.364 --> 00:01:33.501
I followed the beat of my own heart

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.114
and that beat led me here.

00:01:35.114 --> 00:01:36.452
Find your qualities.

00:01:36.452 --> 00:01:38.089
Instead of focusing on the negative,

00:01:38.089 --> 00:01:39.839
which I know can be hard,

00:01:39.839 --> 00:01:41.923
focus on the positive.

00:01:41.923 --> 00:01:43.999
And it doesn't have to
be a physical thing.

00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:46.653
Maybe you're amazing at Mario Kart

00:01:46.653 --> 00:01:49.081
or you're a brilliant pianist,

00:01:49.081 --> 00:01:50.953
an amazing painter, a singer,

00:01:50.953 --> 00:01:53.092
you make great grades at school.

00:01:53.092 --> 00:01:55.594
No one is perfect at everything

00:01:55.594 --> 00:01:58.435
and we're all made to
be perfectly imperfect.

00:01:58.435 --> 00:02:00.613
Kind of like this crystal.

00:02:00.613 --> 00:02:04.293
See, it's not perfectly cut
like a flawless diamond,

00:02:04.293 --> 00:02:07.353
but it's beautiful in its own unique way.

00:02:07.353 --> 00:02:09.234
There won't be another
crystal like this one

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:10.263
and just like you,

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.240
it has many, many facets

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.405
and you'll be discovering
more of them as time goes by

00:02:15.405 --> 00:02:17.306
and if you don't think you have a quality,

00:02:17.306 --> 00:02:19.662
just ask yourself this simple question:

00:02:19.662 --> 00:02:21.300
what am I good at?

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.338
Everyone is good at something

00:02:23.338 --> 00:02:24.853
and if you don't know what it is,

00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:27.755
well, take this opportunity to find it.

00:02:27.755 --> 00:02:31.134
Sign up for cooking
classes, painting classes,

00:02:31.134 --> 00:02:33.303
learn how to sing, play some sports,

00:02:33.303 --> 00:02:35.730
pick up on a passion and nurture it

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.777
because this helps build self-worth,

00:02:37.777 --> 00:02:40.350
it gives you something
to do and strive for.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:44.178
I was rejected but it was the
best rejection ever for me

00:02:44.178 --> 00:02:46.196
to lead me in a different direction,

00:02:46.196 --> 00:02:48.936
the direction where I'm
heading towards right now

00:02:48.936 --> 00:02:52.266
and that was back in 2007,

00:02:52.266 --> 00:02:56.964
I applied for a job at a
counter at department store

00:02:56.964 --> 00:03:00.520
because I really wanted to
work in the beauty industry,

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.992
I wanted to be a makeup artist

00:03:01.992 --> 00:03:04.158
and I wanted to empower women

00:03:04.158 --> 00:03:07.333
through just the art of beauty.

00:03:07.333 --> 00:03:09.057
And so, I went in,

00:03:09.057 --> 00:03:11.067
they were looking for a sales associate

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:12.633
and I applied for the job,

00:03:12.633 --> 00:03:14.091
I filled out the application,

00:03:14.091 --> 00:03:16.163
I did the sit-down interview,

00:03:16.163 --> 00:03:17.783
I answered all the right questions,

00:03:17.783 --> 00:03:19.646
I mean, they were very
impressed with my knowledge

00:03:19.646 --> 00:03:21.121
and my passion

00:03:21.121 --> 00:03:23.224
and the last question she asked me was,

00:03:23.224 --> 00:03:25.260
"Have you ever worked in sales?"

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.891
And I said no, you know,

00:03:26.891 --> 00:03:28.542
I'm a waitress, you know,

00:03:28.542 --> 00:03:29.721
I know how to host,

00:03:29.721 --> 00:03:31.456
how to make people feel good,

00:03:31.456 --> 00:03:33.605
and I know how to really understand

00:03:33.605 --> 00:03:36.223
and read the fine lines
and details of people

00:03:36.223 --> 00:03:37.895
'cause, you know, like,
when you're waiting tables,

00:03:37.895 --> 00:03:39.556
you really have to see,
like, what someone wants

00:03:39.556 --> 00:03:42.305
without them needing
to say anything to you.

00:03:42.305 --> 00:03:44.382
So, it wasn't good enough for her though

00:03:44.382 --> 00:03:45.732
because she said, "Well,

00:03:45.732 --> 00:03:47.464
"unfortunately we do need someone that

00:03:47.464 --> 00:03:49.110
"has experience in sales."

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.875
And I said, but I can learn, you know,

00:03:50.875 --> 00:03:52.156
like, please give me a shot,

00:03:52.156 --> 00:03:54.123
you know, like, just give me a
chance, I'm willing to learn,

00:03:54.123 --> 00:03:56.649
and I know I can sell beauty.

00:03:56.649 --> 00:03:58.467
I mean, I love it, I'm
passionate about it.

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.474
Two weeks later I never got the call back

00:04:00.474 --> 00:04:02.558
and I was really devastated because,

00:04:02.558 --> 00:04:03.825
you know, it's a rejection,

00:04:03.825 --> 00:04:06.462
it's tough because I think

00:04:06.462 --> 00:04:10.136
we're all programmed to
wanting to have, like,

00:04:10.136 --> 00:04:11.442
positive reinforcement, you know,

00:04:11.442 --> 00:04:13.614
we want positive reinforcement,

00:04:13.614 --> 00:04:16.533
we want people to say
yes, we always want yes,

00:04:16.533 --> 00:04:19.258
I mean, no is such a negative,

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:22.515
like, I feel like sometimes
we think no is something bad

00:04:22.515 --> 00:04:25.272
but sometimes we need no's in our lives

00:04:25.272 --> 00:04:27.649
to kind of shift us in
a different direction,

00:04:27.649 --> 00:04:28.482
you know?

00:04:28.482 --> 00:04:31.432
I always find that in
life, like, the universe,

00:04:31.432 --> 00:04:33.649
there's always three answers
when you want something,

00:04:33.649 --> 00:04:35.436
it's either yes,

00:04:35.436 --> 00:04:37.868
not yet, or I have something better.

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:38.743
So, in this case--

00:04:38.743 --> 00:04:40.705
- (all simultaneously) Oh!

00:04:40.705 --> 00:04:41.663
- In this case,

00:04:41.663 --> 00:04:43.975
I knew that there was going
to be something better,

00:04:43.975 --> 00:04:45.939
I didn't take that rejection,

00:04:45.939 --> 00:04:49.222
I didn't just, I didn't
drop my love for beauty,

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:51.776
in fact, I opened another door for myself

00:04:51.776 --> 00:04:54.376
and that was through YouTube, my webcam.

00:04:54.376 --> 00:04:55.488
And I said you know what?

00:04:55.488 --> 00:04:58.527
I may not be able to have
a job as a sales associate

00:04:58.527 --> 00:05:00.498
at a department store selling makeup,

00:05:00.498 --> 00:05:03.118
but at least I can still
fulfill my passion in beauty

00:05:03.118 --> 00:05:05.663
by filming these tutorials
and helping girls

00:05:05.663 --> 00:05:07.629
and inspiring girls to
try new beauty looks

00:05:07.629 --> 00:05:08.960
and that's what I did.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.758
And two years later, Long Comb calls me

00:05:11.758 --> 00:05:13.152
and they wanted me to become

00:05:13.152 --> 00:05:15.653
their official online spokesperson.

00:05:15.653 --> 00:05:16.707
I realized, you know,

00:05:16.707 --> 00:05:19.456
had I have gone back in
time and told myself, hey,

00:05:19.456 --> 00:05:22.220
you know what, this
rejection is something that

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:25.641
you need to take and, you
know, it's not a bad thing.

00:05:25.641 --> 00:05:27.154
I think, like,

00:05:27.154 --> 00:05:28.864
you know, that was the best
thing that ever happened to me

00:05:28.864 --> 00:05:29.921
was that rejection.

00:05:29.921 --> 00:05:31.197
So, I absolutely agree with you, Andrea,

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:34.953
like, sometimes rejection
is a blessing in disguise.

00:05:34.953 --> 00:05:37.594
What do you do when you start
a business but it fails?

00:05:37.594 --> 00:05:41.123
Well, hopefully you can
learn from all the mistakes,

00:05:41.123 --> 00:05:43.169
all the good things,
and all the bad things

00:05:43.169 --> 00:05:45.021
and reapply it to your new business

00:05:45.021 --> 00:05:46.501
or reapply it to your new job

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:48.880
or your new career destination.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:49.943
Look at Apple.

00:05:49.943 --> 00:05:52.049
Apple is one of the most prestigious,

00:05:52.049 --> 00:05:54.803
bankable companies in the world

00:05:54.803 --> 00:05:56.556
and they had a lot of failures,

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.605
they had a lot of
launches that didn't work,

00:05:58.605 --> 00:05:59.728
they had a lot of things that

00:05:59.728 --> 00:06:02.657
just didn't click with the
audience and their customers

00:06:02.657 --> 00:06:05.842
but that didn't stop them from
having the thriving business.

00:06:05.842 --> 00:06:08.842
You learn way more when you
fail than when you succeed.

00:06:08.842 --> 00:06:11.296
That's something I can guarantee you on.

00:06:11.296 --> 00:06:13.207
I didn't prepare myself
to become a beauty guru.

00:06:13.207 --> 00:06:14.040
It didn't just happen,

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.430
it was something that
I knew fit for myself.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:21.849
I started filming on YouTube
on my webcam in college

00:06:21.849 --> 00:06:24.558
in my room, like, just
doing makeup tutorials

00:06:24.558 --> 00:06:27.567
and now, now, like, I work with L'Oreal

00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:30.438
and I have, like, three companies that

00:06:30.438 --> 00:06:32.248
I'm a CEO of,

00:06:32.248 --> 00:06:35.138
so it's incredible how
that all happened because

00:06:35.138 --> 00:06:38.134
I had a passion and it
all started from a webcam.

00:06:38.134 --> 00:06:40.674
And it doesn't matter how
small your beginnings are,

00:06:40.674 --> 00:06:41.669
it doesn't matter,

00:06:41.669 --> 00:06:45.005
it just, all that matters
is how big your passion is.

00:06:45.005 --> 00:06:46.975
If I had to choose one thing
that really motivates me

00:06:46.975 --> 00:06:49.725
that I can recommend to a
lot of young entrepreneurs,

00:06:49.725 --> 00:06:51.370
it's having that,

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:52.878
finding and understanding why

00:06:52.878 --> 00:06:54.280
you're doing what you're doing,

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.662
you know, having a sense of purpose,

00:06:55.662 --> 00:06:58.842
because oftentimes I meet so
many aspiring entrepreneurs

00:06:58.842 --> 00:07:00.279
and they have these great ideas

00:07:00.279 --> 00:07:02.445
but they don't even know
why they're doing it.

00:07:02.445 --> 00:07:05.031
Money should be a byproduct
of what you love to do.

00:07:05.031 --> 00:07:07.583
I just want to really
inspire the youth because

00:07:07.583 --> 00:07:10.296
I've always believed in
teaching and sharing.

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:12.618
Not coming from an
authoritative point of view,

00:07:12.618 --> 00:07:14.390
like, you have to use this or use that,

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:15.915
but this is what works best for me

00:07:15.915 --> 00:07:17.410
and it might work best for you

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:18.675
and if it doesn't work for you,

00:07:18.675 --> 00:07:20.525
then just comment and let me
know what works best for you

00:07:20.525 --> 00:07:21.958
because there might be
someone here watching this

00:07:21.958 --> 00:07:23.462
that we can help.

00:07:23.462 --> 00:07:25.945
My biggest thing I would
tell myself is really

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.343
to just focus on what makes you happy.

00:07:28.343 --> 00:07:29.176
You know, like,

00:07:29.176 --> 00:07:30.618
don't listen to what
everyone else is telling you,

00:07:30.618 --> 00:07:32.600
like, your parents are
pushing you in this direction,

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.996
your friends are trying
to get you to do this,

00:07:34.996 --> 00:07:36.822
ask yourself, look at
yourself in the mirror,

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:39.059
and ask yourself what
do I want for myself?

00:07:39.059 --> 00:07:39.900
You know?

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:41.593
And that was, when I was growing up,

00:07:41.593 --> 00:07:43.379
it was always me pleasing my parents,

00:07:43.379 --> 00:07:45.821
pleasing my friends, trying to fit in,

00:07:45.821 --> 00:07:48.547
but I never once asked
myself what makes me happy,

00:07:48.547 --> 00:07:50.605
what do I want to do?

00:07:50.605 --> 00:07:54.299
And I think my biggest
advice is really just

00:07:54.299 --> 00:07:57.447
taking the time and really
just finding quiet time,

00:07:57.447 --> 00:07:59.574
giving yourself moments to reflect on

00:07:59.574 --> 00:08:03.397
where you want to see
yourself in the next 10 years.

00:08:03.397 --> 00:08:05.044
And really, like, being really realistic,

00:08:05.044 --> 00:08:06.722
not about I want to impress my friends,

00:08:06.722 --> 00:08:09.188
I want to have a nice car,
and have an amazing career,

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:10.892
it's not about what everyone else wants,

00:08:10.892 --> 00:08:12.248
it's about what you want.

00:08:12.248 --> 00:08:13.772
I want to inspire girls and show them that

00:08:13.772 --> 00:08:17.009
you don't have to do one
thing and stick with it,

00:08:17.009 --> 00:08:18.667
like, if you love music,

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:20.074
you don't really need to be a musician

00:08:20.074 --> 00:08:21.046
if you're not a good singer,

00:08:21.046 --> 00:08:22.602
you can manage musicians

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:25.245
or you can work doing, like, sound effects

00:08:25.245 --> 00:08:26.078
or stuff like that.

00:08:26.078 --> 00:08:27.974
There's so many different
things you can do

00:08:27.974 --> 00:08:28.999
that you really love.

00:08:28.999 --> 00:08:30.301
And for me, mine was beauty.

00:08:30.301 --> 00:08:31.733
I love art but I also love beauty

00:08:31.733 --> 00:08:33.972
and I found a way to
combine the two together

00:08:33.972 --> 00:08:35.536
and create makeup tutorials

00:08:35.536 --> 00:08:38.327
and show girls how to
become their own artists

00:08:38.327 --> 00:08:39.653
and become their own makeup artists

00:08:39.653 --> 00:08:40.611
and, in a sense,

00:08:40.611 --> 00:08:43.516
teaching other girls to wake up every day

00:08:43.516 --> 00:08:47.167
and apply a red lipstick
to feel confident again.

00:08:47.167 --> 00:08:48.224
What I recommend usually

00:08:48.224 --> 00:08:49.797
when anyone is starting on YouTube

00:08:49.797 --> 00:08:51.877
is to really focus on storytelling

00:08:51.877 --> 00:08:55.158
because storytelling
has a longer shelf life

00:08:55.158 --> 00:08:57.267
than just doing a funny viral video,

00:08:57.267 --> 00:08:58.215
like, you want to tell stories

00:08:58.215 --> 00:09:00.741
and you want something
that can last longer

00:09:00.741 --> 00:09:02.490
than just a one hit wonder.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:04.675
It's like any business you build, I mean,

00:09:04.675 --> 00:09:06.728
before you start you have to know

00:09:06.728 --> 00:09:08.192
exactly what are you selling,

00:09:08.192 --> 00:09:09.370
what are you projecting,

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.407
what's your message,

00:09:10.407 --> 00:09:12.549
what's your vision, what's
your brand identity?

00:09:12.549 --> 00:09:14.110
And from there, you can work.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.596
I wanted to make this video
to remind you guys that

00:09:16.596 --> 00:09:18.559
it's okay to feel stressed,

00:09:18.559 --> 00:09:19.736
it's very natural,

00:09:19.736 --> 00:09:22.429
but the thing is you can't
feel stressed all the time.

00:09:22.429 --> 00:09:23.730
Even something like this,

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.715
a phone, a machine messes up

00:09:25.715 --> 00:09:27.158
and remember, guys,

00:09:27.158 --> 00:09:29.090
we also have to charge these things,

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:30.834
they don't just run on forever,

00:09:30.834 --> 00:09:32.273
even they need a break.

00:09:32.273 --> 00:09:34.590
And so, if something like
a cell phone, a machine,

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.730
needs a break, imagine us.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:39.627
We need to give ourselves time to relax,

00:09:39.627 --> 00:09:40.920
to recharge,

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.025
to find and seek that inner peace.

00:09:43.025 --> 00:09:45.388
This day and age where
everything is moving so fast

00:09:45.388 --> 00:09:47.772
and we're always wanting
to be in the know,

00:09:47.772 --> 00:09:49.627
we're trying to keep up with everything.

00:09:49.627 --> 00:09:52.462
There's this pressure to always be on

00:09:52.462 --> 00:09:56.629
but there's nothing wrong with
just turning everything off.

00:09:58.076 --> 00:09:59.490
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.893
I made this video because
MJ Illustrates asked me to.

00:10:02.893 --> 00:10:05.100
If there's someone you'd like
to vote on for the next top 10

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:06.612
check out the link in the description

00:10:06.612 --> 00:10:08.479
and go and have your say.

00:10:08.479 --> 00:10:10.862
Finally, I want to give a
quick shout out to Marian Lizzi

00:10:10.862 --> 00:10:13.520
who was my publisher from
Penguin Random House.

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:14.994
Marian, thank you so much for your support

00:10:14.994 --> 00:10:17.085
on this one word book journey

00:10:17.085 --> 00:10:19.680
and I really appreciate the
picture you took on Instagram

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.641
and shared it with your following as well.

00:10:21.641 --> 00:10:22.610
Thank you again.

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:23.882
So, thank you guys again for watching.

00:10:23.882 --> 00:10:25.043
I believe in you,

00:10:25.043 --> 00:10:26.868
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:10:26.868 --> 00:10:29.168
and whatever your one word is,

00:10:29.168 --> 00:10:31.168
much love, see you soon.

00:10:37.564 --> 00:10:40.465
- I know not everyone in
the world has the luxury

00:10:40.465 --> 00:10:43.576
to do their dream job because
they have to make money,

00:10:43.576 --> 00:10:44.409
they have to hustle,

00:10:44.409 --> 00:10:47.667
they have to accept a job
that they might not want to do

00:10:47.667 --> 00:10:48.919
or they hate.

00:10:48.919 --> 00:10:52.586
Every idea has a million
different roadmaps.

00:10:53.429 --> 00:10:54.727
If you love origami,

00:10:54.727 --> 00:10:57.716
have you perhaps thought
about going into engineering,

00:10:57.716 --> 00:10:59.887
learning coding, developing an app,

00:10:59.887 --> 00:11:01.945
designing, even.

00:11:01.945 --> 00:11:04.032
There's so many different
paths that you can take

00:11:04.032 --> 00:11:08.197
and there's no one size fit for
all rule for your dream job.

00:11:08.197 --> 00:11:10.641
There's so many different
things you can do

00:11:10.641 --> 00:11:11.981
with your giftings.

00:11:11.981 --> 00:11:13.733
If you do have a dream job idea,

00:11:13.733 --> 00:11:15.095
have that as a goal

00:11:15.095 --> 00:11:17.225
but leave room for yourself to grow

00:11:17.225 --> 00:11:19.725
and explore different options.

00:11:21.026 --> 00:11:22.455
It's easy, just engage.

00:11:22.455 --> 00:11:24.142
Engage with your viewers.

00:11:24.142 --> 00:11:25.862
Actually go out and talk to them

00:11:25.862 --> 00:11:27.700
and show them that you are talking to them

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:30.237
and you are interested in what they think.

00:11:30.237 --> 00:11:32.922
You just really have to
have a two way conversation

00:11:32.922 --> 00:11:35.283
with the people who are
watching your stuff because

00:11:35.283 --> 00:11:38.396
traditional media, it was
just a one way street.

00:11:38.396 --> 00:11:40.818
With new media, when you're
watching the content,

00:11:40.818 --> 00:11:42.988
you start seeing all these
comments from other viewers

00:11:42.988 --> 00:11:46.529
and that in itself
creates a new content too.

00:11:46.529 --> 00:11:47.934
Sometimes they're debating,

00:11:47.934 --> 00:11:49.483
sometimes they're adding value,

00:11:49.483 --> 00:11:51.342
sometimes it's just really funny comments

00:11:51.342 --> 00:11:54.419
but I think now it's really
just having a social aspect

00:11:54.419 --> 00:11:56.471
to the content that you're creating.

00:11:56.471 --> 00:11:58.684
Consciously, think positive thoughts,

00:11:58.684 --> 00:12:01.301
especially during moments
when you're feeling down.

00:12:01.301 --> 00:12:02.844
So, take a deep breath,

00:12:02.844 --> 00:12:05.841
and remind yourself that life is too short

00:12:05.841 --> 00:12:08.948
and you got to make the best of it.

00:12:08.948 --> 00:12:11.384
Listen to music that will lift your mood.

00:12:11.384 --> 00:12:13.054
A good beat and sound has been proven

00:12:13.054 --> 00:12:15.231
to help people in a positive way.

00:12:15.231 --> 00:12:17.987
Music and sound has been known
to help the growth of plants.

00:12:17.987 --> 00:12:19.387
That says a lot.

00:12:19.387 --> 00:12:21.170
You want to have a healthy habit

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.087
of maintaining this mental muscle

00:12:23.087 --> 00:12:25.235
but you also don't want to overdo it.

00:12:25.235 --> 00:12:27.106
Everything in moderation,

00:12:27.106 --> 00:12:28.481
balance is key.

00:12:28.481 --> 00:12:30.349
It's good to remind
yourself from time to time

00:12:30.349 --> 00:12:33.269
how worthy and how, you
know, awesome you are

00:12:33.269 --> 00:12:36.554
but you also want to leave
room to grow and improve.

00:12:36.554 --> 00:12:40.721
I mean, we can all change
and evolve for the better.

